03); relaxing max_wait to 1200 and even 5000 still fails to reach 1635 (steps 10, 09). The window is also busy overall (8217 events, 1967 active nodes; step_02) and node 302 is a high-degree hub (167 events, 142 partners; step_05) with a large 2-hop neighbourhood (step_04), so static connectivity and popularity \u2014 not genuine temporal propagation \u2014 explain the apparent link. Endpoint activity is sparse and non-synchronised (steps 14, 19). Conclusion: no genuine time-respecting cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_9cf28e7b\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [767, 1635],\n  \"window\": [20674, 59073],\n  \"confidence\": 0.92,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"With the 600-unit relay constraint, node 767's temporal forward reachable set contains only 4 nodes and does not include 1635 (step_01), and no time-respecting path exists (step_08). Node 1635's only in-neighbours in the window are 106, 133 and 302, each with a single incoming event (steps 07, 11-13), and none of these three is reachable from 767 under the 600-unit constraint (steps 15, 17, 18). Confounder controls: a connection does exist when timing is relaxed \u2014 767->722 (t=24954) -> 302 (t=25565) -> 1635 (t=52915) \u2014 but its hop waits are 611 and 27350, i.e. ~46x the allowed delay (step_03); relaxing max_wait to 1200 and even 5000 still fails to reach 1635 (steps 10, 09). The window is also busy overall (8217 events, 1967 active nodes; step_02) and node 302 is a high-degree hub (167 events, 142 partners; step_05) with a large 2-hop neighbourhood (step_04), so static connectivity and popularity \u2014 not genuine temporal propagation \u2014 explain the apparent link. Endpoint activity is sparse and non-synchronised (steps 14, 19). Conclusion: no genuine time-respecting cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 77778, "total_output_tokens": 4350, "total_tokens": 82128, "total_latency_ms": 70552, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}